  "worked_solution": "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6x+{x}^{2},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (6x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$",
